  "final": "Done. Summary of the change:\n\n**`src/numbers.py`** — added `clamp(value, lower, upper)`:\n- Raises `ValueError` when `lower > upper`.\n- Returns `lower` when `value < lower`, `upper` when `value > upper`, otherwise `value` (inclusive bounds; equal bounds are allowed and always return that value).\n- The existing `add` function is preserved unchanged.\n\n**`checks/public.py`** — kept the original `add` check and added clamp coverage: values inside/at both bounds, clamping below and above, degenerate bound (`lower == upper`), float inputs, and three reversed-bound cases that must raise `ValueError`.\n\nVerification: `python3 checks/public.py` prints `All checks passed.` Only files under `src/` and `checks/` were modified.",
